WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.436
-A bombshell new report alleges

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.339
that GOP members of Congress and
Trump administration staffers

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.207
had planning sessions
with organizers

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.876
ahead of the January 6th rally

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.610
that led to the insurrection
at the Capitol.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.680
Meanwhile, human insurrection
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.516
got into yet another
shouting match

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.850
with colleagues
on the House floor.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.019
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.055
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:28.027
After four years of Trump,
I feel like our barometer

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.129
for what counts as a scandal
is a little off.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.298
Trump generated too many
controversies to count,

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:33.533
so we just moved on.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.935
For example, no one seems
to remember or care

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.303
that on top of everything else
he did,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.272
when Trump was president,
the White House accepted

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:42.575
at least 83 separate gifts
from Saudi Arabia, including...

00:00:55.321 --> 00:01:00.059 line:0%
I guess that means they hacked
his Amazon wish list.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.462 line:0%
Were they under the impression
that our president

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:05.598
was the drug dealer
from "Boogie Nights"?

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.667
My only regret is Trump
never showed up to a rally

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:09.836
wearing all of it at once.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.538
[ As Trump ] I killed
this cheetah myself.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.173
Oh, he was fast,
but I was faster.

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:17.177
Ran him down.
Ran him down and skinned him.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:20.680
Of course, my favorite
cheetah -- Chester.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.915
We love Chester Cheetah,
don't we folks?

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.851
With the high-top sneakers
and the cool sunglasses.

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:31.090
First time I met Chester
was in '89 at CBGBs.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.493
And he walked up to me
and he lowered those shades.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:37.997
He lowered them down to the tip
of his chin and nose.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.099
As he said to me, "Sir."

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.567
I'll never forget
what he said to me.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.436
He said, "Sir.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:47.373
It's not easy...being cheesy."

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.574
Truer words.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.143
[ Normal voice ]
And seriously, who thought

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:55.048
giving Donald Trump a dagger
was a good idea?

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.849
The second he unwrapped that,
I bet he started

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.085
running around the White House
Rose Garden like this.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.220
-Let me see what you have.
-A knife.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.190
-No!

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.160
-Melania, had to call up
whoever it was

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.461
that was dumb enough to send it.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.495
"Yep, nope.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.830
Yep, Melania,
we understand now

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.399
that was not a smart gift
to send the president.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.402
Look, we're just glad
everyone is okay.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.338
We promise the next time
we will be best.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:20.639
Is that right?"

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.942
So all kinds of crazy [bleep]
flew under the radar

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.377
during Trump's presidency.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.779
Meanwhile, here's a very real
story about President Biden

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.848
that Politico thought qualified
as news last week.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.049
He swears a lot.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:48.267
The man -- The man is 78.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.102
I think he's old enough
to curse.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.537
I'm in my 40s

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:54.640
and I curse that much
just getting out of a chair.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.275
And are we in high school?

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:59.746
Was this gossip delivered
next to an open locker?

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.948
"Did you hear,
Joe Biden said the word..."

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:09.555
Of course -- Of course
Joe Biden curses.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.156
Nobody says "malarkey"

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:15.528
unless they're trying really
hard not to say "Go get [bleep]"

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.229
The guy's from Scranton,

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:21.700
which is a place for people
not fancy enough for Philly.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.570
"Scranton" even sounds
like a curse word.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.704
"Hey, get off your ass
and do some work,

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:27.974
you Scranton dip-[bleep]"

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.876
He lives in Delaware.
Have you ever been to Delaware?

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.744
When you get off the Amtrak
in Wilmington,

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.447
it's almost impossible
not to say, "Oh [bleep]"

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.649
I have cousins in Delaware,

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.517
and we have multiple
Delawareans on our staff,

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:39.719
so I can make those jokes,

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.220
knowing full well that
the next time I see them,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.221
they will tell me "[Bleep] off."

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.791
It's like how they express love.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.826
I do wish we'd see more of this
version of Joe Biden, though.

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:50.396
Sometimes the soft-talkin' Joe
can be a little unnerving.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.533
He's like a grandpa
in a dystopian YA movie

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.301
who won't admit
how bad things are.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.702
[ As Biden ] It's okay.
We're going to be fine.

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:59.839
We're out of food, but I think
I can talk some sense

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.274
to the Council of Authorium.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:04.210
No one here is gonna have to
compete in the Death Olympics.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.911
No one.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.814
[ Normal voice ] I'd rather Joe
just came out guns blazing,

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.516
flipping people off
at town halls,

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.918
challenging Jake Tapper
to an arm-wrestling match.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:15.454
Just be the grandpa
who goes to Lowe's

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.957
and finds out the cost
of propane went up $1.50.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.726
That's the first time I ever
heard the words "horse [bleep]"

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:23.896
and "kiss my wrinkly old ass"
in the same sentence.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.097
But I get his frustration.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:26.565
Everyone's frustrated
with everything.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:27.366
You can just feel it.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:28.600
People are mad and tired

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.169
after a year and a half
of being cooped up inside

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.437
and Republicans being nutjobs

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.438
and corporate Democrats
making things difficult

00:04:33.438 --> 00:04:34.607
just because they can.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.809
Everyone's exhausted.
Everything's exhausting.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.111
Former President Obama made that
point during a rally in Virginia

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.747
for Democratic gubernatorial
candidate Terry McAuliffe

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:42.581
over the weekend.

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:45.151
-Look, I know a lot of people

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:48.688
are tired of politics right now.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.425
I -- Listen,
I'll make a confession.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:55.528
I never watch political shows.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:58.497
Michelle and I, when we're
at home, you know, I'm reading.

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:01.868
She's watching HGTV,
maybe the food channel.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.903
-Only Obama could get away
with a joke like that.

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:06.205
If I ever said that
about my wife,

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.174
I'd get an icy stare
so haunting,

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.677
it would stay with me
for the rest of my life.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:13.146
I'd have to change stream
mid-conversation.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.681
"Well, I'm the reader
in the family.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:21.587
This one's always
"Keeping Up With --" Dow Jones.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.589
She's very good with money.
I just spend it.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:26.358
But she makes sure we save
for the kids' future."

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.494
But I guess Obama's just
working on some new material,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.962
because ever since he left
the White House,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.697
he's always peppered
some stand-up comedy

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:34.033
into his speeches,
and he did the same in Virginia,

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.502
referencing the fact that
the GOP candidate for governor,

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.170
Glenn Youngkin,
has refused to say

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.205
if he personally supports
same-sex marriage.

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:43.543
-I mean, I understand why people
just feel kind of like,

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:48.648
"Oh, when's this gonna end?"

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:50.849
And sometimes politics
in Washington

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:52.384
feels that way, right?

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:56.922
It's like, are we still arguing
about gay marriage, really?

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.824
I thought that ship had sailed.

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:01.727
[ Stammering ]

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:05.564
I thought that was pretty
clearly the right thing to do.

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.032
[ Stammering ]

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:12.238
We've got Republicans
across the country who said,

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.740
"Yeah, of course,"

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.909
and we're going to
reopen that can up?

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.511
What?

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:21.314
-I love -- I love when
stand-up Obama comes back.

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:25.017
Someone get that man
a brick wall and a cordless mic.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:28.320
He must be working on material
for his new Netflix special,

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.089
"Barack O-No-You-Didn't!"

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.423
[ As Obama ] [ Stammering ]

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:34.993
What's the deal with
cellphones on airplanes?

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:39.932
You're telling me I could call
Beijing from, uh, Air Force One

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.535
but JetBlue won't let me
play "Candy Crush."

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.370
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:50.910
I guess the, uhhhhh,
only thing they want crushed

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.113
is my kneecaps...

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:56.882
when the dummy in front of me...

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:58.618
leans his seat back.

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:04.724
Let's see.
What else? What else?

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.091
[ Normal voice ] Alright,
Obama's in Virginia

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:07.526
because the race for governor
is tight there

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:08.860
and Republicans
are already preparing

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.863
to call any Democratic victory
in that state stolen,

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.498
just like they did
with the 2020 election.

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.233
In fact, former Trump aide
Steve Bannon

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.202
has already said as much,
and last week he invited

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:19.105
MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell
back on his podcast

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:22.542
to float yet another weird claim
about supposed voter fraud --

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:25.611
You can find fraudulent votes
in parking lots.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.780
-Either McAuliffe
is going to lose

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.782
or it's going to be
so tight, right?

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:30.916
You got this thing in Fairfax

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:32.084
where they're trying
to steal it already

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:34.954
because the Biden administration
has collapsed.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:38.357
-The really interesting part is
you can pull a household.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:41.727
If you pull a household
that has five people or below,

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:44.630
it's usually very accurate,
about almost 100%.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.933
You go there, yes, all five
voted, all five live there.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:49.969
You get up to six up to --

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.104
it can go all the way
as high as 300.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:55.741
But let's say you have 20 people
living in this household

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.544
and you look -- or this house
and you look on Google Maps,

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:01.814
'cause the computer pulls it up,
it's a little single dwelling.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.482
Now you go out there

00:08:03.482 --> 00:08:05.318
and you find out
only two people live there,

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.786
but they used all the other
18 people's names

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:08.821
that they pulled there.

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:11.223
Empty parking lots.

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:13.559
I mean, you name it,
it's on there.

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.261
-You know, I'm starting to worry
that Mike Lindell

00:08:16.261 --> 00:08:19.632
is neglecting
his pillow business.

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:21.900
"No, I'm sorry.
Mr. Lindell isn't in right now.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.669
He's on his hands and knees
in the parking lot

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.604
looking for votes.

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:28.341
But, yeah, sure,
I can take a message.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:31.310
Okay. Lumpy.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.079
Smells wet.
Got it. Anything?

00:08:34.079 --> 00:08:36.482
Scratching sound
coming from the inside."

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:38.818
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:41.387
Also, I love how long
his explanation is,

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:44.756
and all it comes down to is
"You go on Google Maps."

00:08:44.756 --> 00:08:47.359
It'd be like your doctor saying,
"We're going to take blood,

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:48.894
run a full set of tests,
get you the MRI,

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:52.632
and then when we have
all the data, we ask Jeeves."

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.199
Seriously, what the hell
is Lindell talking about?

00:08:54.199 --> 00:08:55.968
Does he think people
are committing voter fraud

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.803
because they're getting mail
for old tenants?

00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:01.273
Because if you live in New York,
that's just how it works.

00:09:01.273 --> 00:09:03.643
I didn't vote 18 times,
but I still get mail

00:09:03.643 --> 00:09:06.244
at my apartment
for 18 different people.

00:09:06.244 --> 00:09:07.479
I just got a telegram addressed

00:09:07.479 --> 00:09:09.248
to someone named
Lois Pearlmutter

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:13.686
inviting them to a
"save Penn Station" fundraiser.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.588
Joke for the Jane Jacobs fans.

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:17.223
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:21.927
Republicans are not abandoning
Trump's war on democracy.

00:09:21.927 --> 00:09:24.162
They're embracing it, which is
why it's all the more important

00:09:24.162 --> 00:09:25.331
that we get to the bottom
of what happened

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:26.532
after the last election

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:27.833
before Republicans
try to steal the next one,

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.668
especially after
bombshell new allegations

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.003
reported by "Rolling Stone"
yesterday

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:32.771
in which several
GOP members of Congress

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:35.207
are accused of holding dozens
of planning sessions

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:37.176
with the organizers
of the January 6th rallies

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:38.377
that ultimately led

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.111
to the violent insurrection
at the Capitol.

00:09:40.111 --> 00:09:42.281
-A January 6th bombshell.

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:44.015
"Rolling Stone" magazine
reporting

00:09:44.015 --> 00:09:46.485
that organizers
of the Capitol rally that day

00:09:46.485 --> 00:09:49.154
had been promised
a "blanket pardon"

00:09:49.154 --> 00:09:50.656
by a U.S. congressman.

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:53.626
-"Rolling Stone" reports
Arizona congressman Paul Gosar

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:55.561
gave protest organizers
the impression

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:57.796
that he had spoken
to then-President Trump

00:09:57.796 --> 00:10:00.365
about the pardons
for an unrelated investigation.

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:02.568
-The organizers said
they allegedly spoke to

00:10:02.568 --> 00:10:06.205
"a dozen U.S. representatives
or their teams."

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:08.707
They named
Representative Paul Gosar

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:11.010
and Representative
Andy Biggs of Arizona,

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.378
Representative
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:13.546
of Georgia,

00:10:13.546 --> 00:10:15.647
Representative Lauren Boebert
of Colorado,

00:10:15.647 --> 00:10:18.083
Madison Cawthorn
of North Carolina,

00:10:18.083 --> 00:10:22.287
Louie Gohmert of Texas,
and Mo Brooks of Alabama,

00:10:22.287 --> 00:10:24.590
all Republican congressmen
and -women.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.425
Right now, we don't know
what was discussed

00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:28.393
with each representative
by those planners.

00:10:28.393 --> 00:10:31.330
But the organizers gave
"Rolling Stone" an example

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.531
with Representative Gosar,

00:10:32.531 --> 00:10:34.499
who's saying he offered them
the possibility

00:10:34.499 --> 00:10:37.670
of receiving a "blanket pardon"

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:40.472
to motivate them
to plan the rallies.

00:10:40.472 --> 00:10:43.175
-Geez. Everyone was in on this.
Was Lindell there, too?

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:44.744
[ As Lindell ]
I found a fake ballot

00:10:44.744 --> 00:10:47.646
in the parking lot of a CVS.

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:52.818
This guy voted three times
for someone named Trojan Magnum.

00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:54.887
[ Laughter ]

00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:57.490
[ Normal voice ] Blanket pardon
sounds like the kind of made-up

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.725
fake legal things
these doofuses would say.

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:01.093
It's a weird feature
of our politics

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:02.228
that the most sinister
characters

00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:03.729
are also the biggest morons.

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.297
You could just imagine
Paul Gosar

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:06.866
or Marjorie Taylor Greene
on the phone

00:11:06.866 --> 00:11:08.333
with the January 6th idiots

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:11.136
huddled in their weird little
militia hideout/treehouse,

00:11:11.136 --> 00:11:12.637
promise them all kinds
of crazy [bleep]

00:11:12.637 --> 00:11:14.006
"You didn't hear from me,

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:16.542
but I spoke to the chief wizard
of the Supreme Court,

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:18.077
and he said there's
a secret provision

00:11:18.077 --> 00:11:20.812
written by
Benjamin Franklin's ghost,

00:11:20.812 --> 00:11:22.214
and it says you can have
a blanket pardon,

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:25.851
a private plane, and a $100
gift card to Golden Corral."

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.420
And if you don't remember
Paul Gosar,

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.753
he's the guy who's so crazy,

00:11:28.753 --> 00:11:31.190
six of his siblings
famously endorsed his opponent,

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.625
and he recently claimed
that secret sources

00:11:33.625 --> 00:11:35.927
inside something called
the CIA fraud department

00:11:35.927 --> 00:11:37.430
told him
the election was stolen.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.997
-Here's what he said
about two weeks

00:11:38.997 --> 00:11:42.134
before Republicans in his state
announced they had found nothing

00:11:42.134 --> 00:11:44.136
but additional votes
for Joe Biden

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:47.272
in their bogus and expensive
audit of election results

00:11:47.272 --> 00:11:49.875
in Arizona's
most populous county.

00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:53.612
-We can do that and follow
through on this audit.

00:11:53.612 --> 00:11:57.082
Folks, if it's
what I've been told,

00:11:57.082 --> 00:12:00.953
and I had people come to me
early hours of the day after

00:12:00.953 --> 00:12:03.222
from the Security Exchange
fraud department

00:12:03.222 --> 00:12:05.490
to the CIA fraud department,

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.027
that between 450,000
and 700,000 ballots

00:12:08.027 --> 00:12:09.929
were altered
in the state of Arizona.

00:12:09.929 --> 00:12:11.931
-First,
the CIA fraud department --

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.967
not a thing, doesn't exist.

00:12:14.967 --> 00:12:16.268
-Exactly.

00:12:16.268 --> 00:12:20.105
The greatest trick the
CIA fraud department ever pulled

00:12:20.105 --> 00:12:22.874
was convincing the world
they didn't exist.

00:12:22.874 --> 00:12:25.377
Gosar does seem like the
kind of guy who's on the phone

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:27.913
with other fraud departments
a fair amount.

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:30.148
"Well, the thing is, someone
from your bank e-mailed me

00:12:30.148 --> 00:12:31.584
for my Social Security number.

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.919
So I do think you're responsible
for my identity being stolen.

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:35.420
Who from your bank?

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:38.623
Your mascot, Chase-ter Cheetah.

00:12:38.623 --> 00:12:40.993
He's not your mascot?"

00:12:40.993 --> 00:12:44.930
Again, this is
the fun thing, right?

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.365
Like, when there's no audience,

00:12:46.365 --> 00:12:47.966
you're like, "Yeah,
Chester Cheetah's gonna kill.

00:12:47.966 --> 00:12:49.100
We'll call it back.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.737
They'll carry me out
on their shoulders."

00:12:51.737 --> 00:12:53.839
And then the show ends and we go
back in the dressing room

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:55.073
and we're like,
"That callback worked."

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:56.842
And they're like, "Yeah, yeah."

00:12:56.842 --> 00:13:01.446
Now -- Now we're finding out,
you guys, we are --

00:13:01.446 --> 00:13:03.081
We're finding out, in a way...

00:13:03.081 --> 00:13:06.318
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:06.318 --> 00:13:08.921
In a way, you are
the CIA fraud department.

00:13:08.921 --> 00:13:10.555
[ Laughter ]

00:13:10.555 --> 00:13:12.625
And you just exposed that joke.

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.860
[ Laughter ]

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.194
And it also wouldn't surprise me

00:13:16.194 --> 00:13:17.796
if Marjorie Taylor Greene
was involved in all this.

00:13:17.796 --> 00:13:19.932
She, of course, was a vocal
backer of Trump's "big lie"

00:13:19.932 --> 00:13:22.000
and the ensuing attempt to
overthrow the election results.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.536
And last week,
when the House voted

00:13:23.536 --> 00:13:24.836
to hold Steve Bannon in contempt

00:13:24.836 --> 00:13:26.772
for refusing to comply
with the subpoena,

00:13:26.772 --> 00:13:28.541
she got into yet another
shouting match

00:13:28.541 --> 00:13:29.675
with some of her colleagues.

00:13:29.675 --> 00:13:31.743
-Yesterday, we saw
conspiracy theorist

00:13:31.743 --> 00:13:34.312
and Republican congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:13:34.312 --> 00:13:35.681
Republican of Georgia,

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:38.884
approach and accost
Congresswoman Liz Cheney.

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.953
-This happened during the debate

00:13:40.953 --> 00:13:43.955
over the criminal contempt
referral of Steve Bannon,

00:13:43.955 --> 00:13:48.026
and Taylor Greene walked behind
Congresswoman Liz Cheney

00:13:48.026 --> 00:13:50.662
and Congressman Jamie Raskin
during that debate

00:13:50.662 --> 00:13:54.566
and basically accused them
of making too much out of this

00:13:54.566 --> 00:13:57.369
and saying that they were
focused on the wrong things.

00:13:57.369 --> 00:14:00.271
It delved into a shouting match
on some level

00:14:00.271 --> 00:14:01.773
between the three of them

00:14:01.773 --> 00:14:05.477
and Liz Cheney actually calling
Marjorie Taylor Greene a joke

00:14:05.477 --> 00:14:07.413
and bringing up the fact
that she had talked

00:14:07.413 --> 00:14:09.915
about Jewish space lasers
at one point,

00:14:09.915 --> 00:14:13.184
a claim that Greene
very much denies.

00:14:13.184 --> 00:14:15.186
-Greene yelled back
that she never said that

00:14:15.186 --> 00:14:17.189
and called Cheney a joke.

00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:20.525
-It's not great when you start
a confrontation with someone

00:14:20.525 --> 00:14:22.427
and have to end it by insisting

00:14:22.427 --> 00:14:26.398
you never claimed wildfires were
started by Jewish space lasers.

00:14:26.398 --> 00:14:28.133
It's getting harder
and harder to articulate

00:14:28.133 --> 00:14:29.601
just how unhinged
the right has become.

00:14:29.601 --> 00:14:31.269
They're now claiming
they're vindicated

00:14:31.269 --> 00:14:32.771
by everything
from secret sources

00:14:32.771 --> 00:14:34.539
inside fake
CIA fraud departments

00:14:34.539 --> 00:14:37.008
to proof of voter fraud
found in empty parking lots.

00:14:37.008 --> 00:14:38.810
And they're not going to stop.
They're doubling down.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.712
And new reporting continues
to link them

00:14:40.712 --> 00:14:42.647
directly to attempts
to overthrow our democracy.

00:14:42.647 --> 00:14:44.716
These people need to be told,
in no uncertain terms...

00:14:44.716 --> 00:14:45.918
-No!

00:14:45.918 --> 00:14:49.388
[ Laughter ]

00:14:49.388 --> 00:14:52.591
Didn't see that one coming.
This has been "A Closer Look."

